### Complexity
* **Time Complexity**: $\mathcal{O}(n \log n)$ where $n$ is the number of nodes in the tree. Extracting the in-order traversal takes $\mathcal{O}(n)$, and counting inversions using merge sort takes $\mathcal{O}(n \log n)$.
* **Space Complexity**: $\mathcal{O}(n)$ to store the in-order traversal array and temporary merge buffers.
